        "id": "cog-ln-3",
        "name": "Liboke (Fish in Banana Leaf)",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "servings": 4,
        "prepTime": 15,
        "cookTime": 30,
        "ingredients": [
          "4 whole tilapia or catfish",
          "Banana leaves",
          "Tomato",
          "Onion",
          "Garlic",
          "Ginger",
          "Hot pepper",
          "Salt",
          "Lemon"
        ],
        "instructions": [
          "Clean fish, season with lemon, salt, garlic, ginger",
          "Layer banana leaves, place fish on top",
          "Add sliced tomato, onion, pepper",
          "Wrap tightly in banana leaves, tie with string",
          "Grill or steam 25-30 min",
          "Unwrap at the table",
          "Serve with fufu or cassava"
        ],
        "description": "Fish steamed in banana leaves — the leaf imparts a subtle green flavor and keeps everything moist. A classic Congo River preparation."
      },
      {
        "id": "cog-ln-4",
        "name": "Poulet Moambé (Chicken in Palm Butter Sauce)",
        "difficulty": "Medium",
        "servings": 6,
        "prepTime": 20,
        "cookTime": 45,
        "ingredients": [
          "1 whole chicken (cut into pieces)",
          "1 can palm butter (moambé sauce) or 300ml palm cream",
          "Tomato paste",
          "Onion, garlic",
          "Palm oil",
          "Okra (optional)",
          "Spinach or cassava leaves",
          "Chili pepper",
          "Salt, Maggi cube"
        ],
        "instructions": [
          "Brown chicken pieces in palm oil",
          "Sauté onion and garlic, add tomato paste",
          "Add palm butter/moambé — this is the soul of the dish, a thick, orange, nutty sauce",
          "Add water to thin slightly, add Maggi cube, chili",
          "Simmer chicken in sauce 30-40 min until tender and sauce is thick and rich",
          "Add okra or greens in last 10 min",
          "The sauce should coat the back of a spoon — thick, orange-red, aromatic",
          "Serve with fufu (cassava) or rice",
          "This is Congo's number one dish — every family has their version"
        ],
        "description": "The dish that both Congos claim as their own — chicken simmered in palm butter sauce until the rich, orange moambé coats everything. Considered one of Africa's greatest dishes, poulet moambé videos consistently go viral for the dramatic color and the communal fufu-dipping style of eating.",
